00:52:00.000 --> 00:53:04.000
stated Stena was driven by the desire for fame, possibly the same that his brother received after surviving his ordeal. To guarantee he wouldn't profit from his story, Carey Stena was required to sign a $10 million restitution order to go to the Joey Armstrong Memorial Fund. To spare her family any further distress, he was forbidden from ever speaking, writing, or communicating with anyone about her death. The Sun and Palosso families both filed wrongful death suits against the Cedar Lodge and Carey Stena. It questioned why Carol, Julie, and Sylvina were put in a remote room with few other guests nearby, why Stena was allowed to wonder the grounds unsupervised with a master key and whether there was an adequate lock system on the hotel room door.

